  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence is that the best configuration so far is config_019: multimodal, multiprofile, PCA RNA, ResNet50, avgpool, weighted fusion, with validation accuracy 0.639 and F1 0.6197. Transformer aggregation appears harmful, weighted fusion is better than concat, and ResNet50/ViT are similar, with ResNet50 slightly better. The main remaining uncertainty in this strong setting is whether a learned RNA encoder can improve on PCA, since RNA-only scGPT was weaker than PCA but scVI has not been tested. config_031 tests scVI_n200 while keeping the same multimodal, multiprofile, ResNet50, avgpool, and weighted-fusion design, so it isolates the RNA representation choice. This is the best next experiment because it is a clean one-factor extension of the current best direction: it may find a better model or efficiently confirm that PCA is already sufficient before spending budget on more complex RNA encoders."
}

